WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:54.470
<b>Love Song</b>

3
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.180
Eneru's been up there for a while.

4
00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.600
He must have taken
the golden bell by now.

5
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.830
No matter hard you stretch your arms,
there's no way you can reach up there.

6
00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:03.090
If he took it, I'm gonna take it back!

7
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:04.090
Gimme the waver!

8
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.810
Even Heaven's Gate was blown
away in the twinkling of an eye.

9
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.120
Angel Island.
It's completely destroyed.

10
00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:28.580
But what are we supposed to do?

11
00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.160
And where do we go?

12
00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:33.850
To Cloud End, and then down to the
Blue Sea like Captain McKinley said!

13
00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.070
It's our only choice.

14
00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.450
Hold on.

15
00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.060
There are still a lot of people
in the White-White Sea

16
00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:39.600
who haven't been evacuated yet!

17
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.730
The Milky Roads
leading there've been destroyed!

18
00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.430
They're gone!

19
00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.210
I don't know how we can bring
those ships down without them!

20
00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.750
So you're saying we
just leave those people to die?

21
00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.670
We're all doomed.

22
00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:12.130
The White-White Sea is lost.

23
00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:18.720
Skypiea... it's fading away.

24
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.900
So this is it.

25
00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:40.130
Splendid!

26
00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.460
At last!

27
00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:47.370
The grand belfry that was once the pride
of the legendary city of Shandora!

28
00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:49.810
Now it's mine!

29
00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:53.310
A prize befitting a god
of my power and glory!

30
00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:56.310
The fabled bell, the one
that heralded the start

31
00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:58.710
of this land's 400-year old conflict.

32
00:03:58.710 --> 00:03:59.970
Watch out!

33
00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.300
Something's falling toward us again!

34
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.090
– Wait, it's...
– Take cover!

35
00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:09.940
A leaf?

36
00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:11.980
Huh?

37
00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:16.320
Hey, look!

38
00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.450
There's something written on it.

39
00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.780
It's a message! From Nami and Luffy!

40
00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.700
Huh?

41
00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.870
What's it say?

42
00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:30.830
"Cut down this beanstalk and make
sure it falls toward the west."

43
00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.030
What?!

44
00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:35.280
But... What'll

45
00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:55.390
I've accomplished all
of my objectives but one.

46
00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:56.520
So now...

47
00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:04.330
It's time I destroyed this pathetic land
and the Cumuloregalis Clouds it rests on,

48
00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.200
and set off for the Endless Vearth.

49
00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:14.440
I'm actually gonna miss toying
with the Skypieans' lives!

50
00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:19.550
Eneru!

51
00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.820
Damn him.

52
00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.060
Do you see that?

53
00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:26.860
This one's even bigger!

54
00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:34.050
Maybe we should get out of here wh-while
there's still some place to get!

55
00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.940
Say goodbye, Skypiea!

56
00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:47.900
It's even bigger than his last one!

57
00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:49.360
That bastard!

58
00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.990
Now that he's got his grubby
hands on the golden bell,

59
00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:53.500
he has no more use for Skypiea!

60
00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.290
We can't let him get away with this!

61
00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:00.460
Wait, "we"?
But weren't you gonna escape?

62
00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.760
Yeah, well...

63
00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.810
I can't leave now with what's at stake.

64
00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.050
Besides, you want to
ring that golden bell, right?

65
00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:07.440
I've gotta!

66
00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.610
For Old Timer!

67
00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.780
But... with your arm,
you can't drive the waver.

68
00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:16.080
If I left you here,
you'd keep trying to jump up,

69
00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.490
so leave the driving to me
and I'll get you up there.

70
00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.330
Listen.

71
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.840
You've got to promise that you'll get
us out of this mess in one piece, okay?

72
00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.380
Yeah. You got it!

73
00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:30.550
And thanks!

74
00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:37.130
We've only got one
chance to get this thing right!

75
00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:42.350
I just hope they got my message and
understand what we're attempting to do.

76
00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.970
Let me get this straight!

77
00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:48.600
They're gonna jump to the ark
from the falling beanstalk?

78
00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.890
You got any better ideas?

79
00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:53.150
Well that's crazy.
They can't be serious.

80
00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:55.980
Fine, then I'll leave it to you
to climb up there and stop Luffy.

81
00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:57.280
He won't listen!

82
00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:01.050
Look, I don't care how crazy it sounds!

83
00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.090
We have no choice!

84
00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:03.550
We've gotta let him do this!

85
00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:07.280
Wh-What the...?

86
00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:08.270
Long nose!

87
00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:09.860
I got 'em!

88
00:07:11.320 --> 00:07:15.640
If we stay here, we're just gonna get
pushed down to the ruins below! Run!

89
00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.430
Get away from the beanstalk!

90
00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.270
I'll take care of it!

91
00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.000
All I need to do is cut the vine
down toward that ship, right?

92
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.390
But...!

93
00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:26.230
That maniac is about
to wipe this land away,

94
00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:29.730
and there are only two people who can
reach him before he sets that thing off!

95
00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:30.810
Zoro, wait!

96
00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.940
Nami! Luffy! Ya better get ready!

97
00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:40.650
It's far too late to change things now.

98
00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:46.540
The minute you entered the survival
game, your fates were cast in stone.

99
00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.790
Anything you do is futile.

100
00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:55.090
O-Okay, he's gonna be just fine.

101
00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:58.470
Zoro buddy, you're the
only one who can do this!

102
00:07:58.470 --> 00:07:59.800
It's up to you!

103
00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:07.270
Eneru, I am so sick of you!

104
00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.690
All right! He did it!

105
00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.650
Zoro!

106
00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.170
Insolent little worm.

107
00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.170
He did it!

108
00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:45.170
He did it and got zapped.

109
00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.840
But he did it!

110
00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.220
Oh, no. The vine!

111
00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:54.360
The vine's not falling!

112
00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:55.810
But he cut it!

113
00:08:56.530 --> 00:08:58.990
What is that thing made out of?

114
00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:02.370
It looks like a plant,
but it's solid as a rock!

115
00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:03.740
Pathetic!

116
00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.330
This is what you outsiders
get for butting in!

117
00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.910
Wyper, what are you doing?

118
00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:10.370
Quiet!

119
00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:15.620
We Shandorians are the descendents
of Kalgara, not that kid in the straw hat!

120
00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.670
If anyone is to ring that bell,
it should rightfully be us!

121
00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:20.040
Don't listen to him, Robin!

122
00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.460
He's too banged-up to stop us!

123
00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.380
Besides, Nami and Luffy
are counting on us!

124
00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:27.670
Our only priority right now
is knocking that thing down!

125
00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:31.130
Speaking of which, Zoro's already
cut through half of the stem!

126
00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.500
It probably shouldn't take much
to cut through the rest of it!

127
00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:37.840
My awesome Dance of the Exploding
Stars should do the trick!

128
00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:44.140
After just one little hit, even a gentle
breeze will knock that thing over!

129
00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.010
Once again, it's up to me!

130
00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:48.890
The last line of defense
in our merry band!

131
00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:51.560
Robin, leave all the
dangerous stuff to me!

132
00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.150
You tend to our fallen comrades!

133
00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.240
They look like an oak leaf mochi cake.

134
00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:57.400
Forward!

135
00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.940
About that bell...

136
00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:08.770
Four hundred years ago,
an explorer from my world

137
00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:12.650
said he stumbled upon a city of gold.

138
00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:14.780
People laughed at him
and called him a liar.

139
00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.870
But he has a descendent today
who still believes the stories,

140
00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:22.080
and has spent years searching the Blue
Sea for any evidence of this City of Gold.

141
00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:32.970
If that golden bell can be rung,

142
00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:37.030
everyone will know the City of Gold
is in the sky and not a myth.

143
00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.700
That's the reason Luffy's up there.

144
00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.120
Now do you understand?

145
00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:42.910
Exploding Star!

146
00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:45.620
Noble, isn't it?

147
00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:49.330
Trying to vindicate a man he never met?

148
00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.730
He's had chances to escape.

149
00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:54.730
But he's stuck around
to see this thing through.

150
00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.590
That guy's nuts!

151
00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.600
Rolling Exploding Star!

152
00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.760
Usopp Rubber Band of Doom!

153
00:11:02.270 --> 00:11:03.390
Regular Exploding Star!

154
00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:17.130
What... What is the name
of this explorer's descendent?

155
00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.430
Montblanc Cricket. Why?

156
00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.680
The name of his ancestor who came here.

157
00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.580
Please tell me.

158
00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.590
Was it Noland?

159
00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.250
How...?

160
00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:34.470
Wyper?

161
00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:37.080
What's going on?

162
00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:38.580
Why are you crying?

163
00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:43.080
Is this a sign from you?

164
00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:45.540
Or a miracle?

165
00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.210
What is it, Great Warrior Kalgara?

166
00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.030
Come, Nola!

167
00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:56.900
We'll ring the bell again today so
the sound reaches the ends of the earth!

168
00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:01.560
Let's send the sound you love
to say hello to our friend Noland!

169
00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.850
What the...?

170
00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:38.900
What just did that?

171
00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.700
Guess it doesn't matter, 'cause it
couldn't even budge that beanstalk!

172
00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:46.030
Maybe one of my triple
explosions will do the trick.

173
00:12:46.030 --> 00:12:47.860
– Move.
– Hey!

174
00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.050
Reject!

175
00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.850
What the heck was that?!

176
00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:13.860
Wyper!

177
00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:19.320
That fool. A reject dial.

178
00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.910
Now fall, Giant Jack! Fall!

179
00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.080
Guys! We've got to run away!

180
00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:42.220
This is it! Get on, Luffy!

181
00:13:42.940 --> 00:13:44.400
Gun it! Go!

182
00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:49.300
I should mention,
I've never revved this waver's

183
00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.680
jet dial up to maximum power before.

184
00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.600
I was a little scared
to see how fast it would go.

185
00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:58.940
I guess we're gonna find out now if it'll
be too strong for me to control, huh?

186
00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:00.230
Go for it, Nami!

187
00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.400
Okay!

188
00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:06.620
Hang on, Luffy!

189
00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.030
I am!

190
00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.730
It's falling!

191
00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:18.340
He's right!

192
00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:21.210
What's going on up there?

193
00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.960
Well, Nami, Luffy.

194
00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:24.420
Good luck!

195
00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.760
We're counting on you!

196
00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:29.220
If we let this place be destroyed, we'll
never get to ring that bell, and Cricket

197
00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.390
will never hear it!

198
00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.170
He helped us, so we gotta help him!

199
00:14:32.170 --> 00:14:34.090
Ring that bell and ring it loud!

200
00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:38.170
Jump to Eneru's ship and stop that guy!

201
00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:40.800
Do it!

202
00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:43.610
Everything's up to you
guys now, you got it?

203
00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:44.900
Do it!

204
00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:50.890
My, my.

205
00:14:56.150 --> 00:15:01.070
Now why can't you wait for the completion
of Raigo like the rest of the insects?

206
00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:03.620
Their impatience will be their undoing.

207
00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:06.830
Very well, then.

208
00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:17.420
That you should even
try to reach me now

209
00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:20.640
is insolent far beyond
the point of stupidity!

210
00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:22.640
Now pay for your folly!

211
00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:24.740
Mamaragan!

212
00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.780
That creep!

213
00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.950
He's trying to destroy
the base of the beanstalk!

214
00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:41.530
Do something, Nami!

215
00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.740
Like what?

216
00:15:42.740 --> 00:15:45.830
We're going too fast
and we're too high up!

217
00:15:45.830 --> 00:15:49.960
If this thing loses its foundation,
it'll crash before we get to the top!

218
00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:52.960
We won't reach Eneru,
and we'll fall to our deaths!

219
00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:56.310
Upper Yard's being pummeled!

220
00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.730
This is the end!

221
00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:10.680
Lightning may not harm you, but your
abilities are absolutely useless

222
00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.550
if you can't reach Maxim!

223
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.850
Now fall and face destruction
with the rest of Skypiea!

224
00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:19.190
Say goodbye, boy!

225
00:16:29.010 --> 00:16:31.890
Upper Yard is crumbling.

226
00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:37.020
Luffy! Nami!

227
00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.250
You know...

228
00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.460
I think he's trying to make sure
you don't get near him again!

229
00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:48.290
Too bad! He's mine!

230
00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:54.050
He's destroying the cloud
cover over the ruins!

231
00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:00.510
He plans to destroy the ground itself!

232
00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:04.710
But Wyper's lying
on the ground down there!

233
00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:08.060
So is Zoro! That bastard!

234
00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.310
The ruins...

235
00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:20.650
It won't

236
00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:26.100
This city will never fall to you.

237
00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:29.240
Wyper!

238
00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.890
This land of Shandora was home
to a proud race of warriors.

239
00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.690
This ancient city preserves
and protects their memory.

240
00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:47.030
What's more, their memory
protects this city.

241
00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:49.610
That mighty power
will never fall to you.

242
00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:53.120
No matter how much forest you burn.

243
00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:05.330
won't fall!

244
00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:17.660
No! Wyper!

245
00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:20.580
– It's too dangerous!
– Ah! Let me go! Wyper!

246
00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:23.670
Eh?

247
00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.340
I can still hear the little
fools whining down below.

248
00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:07.710
The Vearth. Of course!

249
00:19:16.350 --> 00:19:17.930
It didn't fall!

250
00:19:17.930 --> 00:19:20.390
Upper Yard is still standing!

251
00:19:25.090 --> 00:19:27.180
Its power is unbelievable!

252
00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:34.320
It must be.

253
00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:36.610
The Vearth is so powerful.

254
00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:42.580
What fools we've been!

255
00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.610
It was never something
to be fought over!

256
00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:48.160
We've spilled so much blood.

257
00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:51.830
And lost so many countless lives.

258
00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:56.500
How could we be so blind for 400 years?

259
00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.890
Wyper!

260
00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.940
Wyper!

261
00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.270
Get outta there!
The beanstalk's coming down!

262
00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.480
Come on, this way,
let's move it! Move it!

263
00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:14.350
Now go!

264
00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:22.270
Go! Straw Hat!

265
00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:29.230
Here I come, Eneru!

266
00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:34.570
Those fools never learn.

267
00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:36.860
Give back the Golden Bell!

268
00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:39.410
Right now!

269
00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.120
That's enough!

270
00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:44.910
It's ready!

271
00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:50.790
Now disappear along with this land!

272
00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:55.610
Raigo!

273
00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.790
Thanks for your help.

274
00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.340
It won't be for nothing!

275
00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.430
Luffy! Wait!

276
00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.470
The ark's over there!

277
00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:33.850
No! Don't do it, please!

278
00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:39.280
The air currents and lightning
discharges in there could kill even you!

279
00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:43.450
What do you think you can do
against this kind of power?

280
00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:44.530
Man of rubber!

281
00:22:38.860 --> 00:22:41.360
You with your thunder and lightning!

282
00:22:41.360 --> 00:22:43.440
We made it all the way to sky island,

283
00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:46.200
and you had to come along
and ruin the weather!

284
00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:49.060
You electrical freak!

285
00:22:51.910 --> 00:22:54.910
Uh, what's with all the
crazy lightning bolts?

286
00:22:56.920 --> 00:22:58.580
I forgot!

287
00:22:58.580 --> 00:23:01.880
That gold ball stuck on his
arm is a natural conductor!

288
00:23:04.470 --> 00:23:06.020
Well then.

289
00:23:06.020 --> 00:23:08.770
I'll just drop it before you
can discharge the electricity!

290
00:23:11.480 --> 00:23:14.110
Let everything be destroyed!

291
00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:18.790
Captain McKinley!

292
00:23:19.130 --> 00:23:20.420
Please stop it!

293
00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:21.500
This is God's land!

294
00:23:21.850 --> 00:23:23.060
It is pointless!

295
00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:25.060
I don't care if it's pointless.

296
00:23:25.060 --> 00:23:29.100
It's the only thing people can do when
they're caught between life and death.

297
00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:30.180
Don't you see?

298
00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:34.850
We've abandoned our home
and chosen to live.

299
00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:36.390
We can't go back.

300
00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:37.890
Nor can we go forward.

301
00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:41.640
Praying.

302
00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:42.850
Is all that we can do.

303
00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:47.860
The song of the island.

304
00:23:48.650 --> 00:23:53.610
When our ears hear that again,
the war will have ended.

305
00:23:57.870 --> 00:23:59.920
I wonder...

306
00:23:59.920 --> 00:24:01.250
Are we all doomed?

307
00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:07.750
Maybe, if I'd had the courage
to stand up to Eneru...

308
00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:10.380
...our friends would have
been spared all this.

309
00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:13.060
Oh, Suu...

310
00:24:13.810 --> 00:24:14.890
Suu?

311
00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:17.480
Does God exist?

312
00:24:18.190 --> 00:24:19.690
If He does...

313
00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:22.770
...why doesn't he save us?

314
00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:24.520
Suu.

315
00:24:25.240 --> 00:24:28.320
Please. If You do exist...

316
00:24:29.100 --> 00:24:33.400
...You must protect those
brave people and keep them safe!

317
00:24:33.410 --> 00:24:35.700
Please! Give us a miracle!

318
00:24:36.280 --> 00:24:39.240
Protect this land, Lord God!

319
00:25:12.490 --> 00:25:14.990
That mass of thunderclouds
has vanished!

320
00:25:15.390 --> 00:25:16.930
What could've happened?

321
00:25:35.670 --> 00:25:39.050
Yeah! It's him, Luffy!

322
00:25:39.050 --> 00:25:41.350
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah!

323
00:25:49.940 --> 00:25:52.320
Now ring it, Straw Hat!

324
00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:55.370
Light the fire of Shandora!

325
00:25:55.780 --> 00:25:57.400
Go, Luffy! Go, Luffy!

326
00:25:57.400 --> 00:25:59.250
Let me hear it, Straw Hat!

327
00:25:59.250 --> 00:26:00.570
The song of the island!

328
00:26:03.480 --> 00:26:06.270
You destroyed my Raigo!

329
00:26:06.910 --> 00:26:07.870
You're next!

330
00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:11.780
I'll ring you along with the bell!

331
00:26:11.780 --> 00:26:13.400
Impudent fool!

332
00:26:17.490 --> 00:26:21.240
Two hundred million volt...

333
00:26:27.400 --> 00:26:28.730
What the hell is that?

334
00:26:29.220 --> 00:26:30.600
Ring the bell?

335
00:26:30.600 --> 00:26:33.020
Is that what you said?

336
00:26:33.020 --> 00:26:34.980
You must be one of
those fools who believes

337
00:26:34.980 --> 00:26:37.070
in the old legend
that when the bell rings,

338
00:26:37.070 --> 00:26:42.150
it will mean the end of the war
between Skypiea and Shandora!

339
00:26:42.150 --> 00:26:44.070
I am God!

340
00:26:49.260 --> 00:26:51.140
I don't care how strong you are.

341
00:26:51.970 --> 00:26:54.390
You're still just a Paramecia type!

342
00:26:54.390 --> 00:26:59.350
You could never match the might of my
Logia power no matter how hard you try!

343
00:26:59.350 --> 00:27:01.190
No matter what you might do!

344
00:27:04.100 --> 00:27:06.810
That won't work on me!

345
00:27:07.820 --> 00:27:10.650
And quit calling yourself God!

346
00:27:10.650 --> 00:27:14.410
What kind of god destroys
everything and saves nothing?

347
00:27:14.410 --> 00:27:15.570
Fake!

348
00:27:26.650 --> 00:27:28.000
was very agile of you.

349
00:27:28.000 --> 00:27:30.040
You grabbed it before
you could be impaled.

350
00:27:30.040 --> 00:27:31.420
Luffy!

351
00:27:33.500 --> 00:27:35.170
But what will you do now?

352
00:27:35.170 --> 00:27:36.840
You have nowhere to run!

353
00:27:38.210 --> 00:27:40.220
The pull of the golden ball on your arm

354
00:27:40.220 --> 00:27:42.890
will draw you deeper and
deeper onto my trident!

355
00:27:42.890 --> 00:27:46.230
And if you should let go,
you'll fall to your death below!

356
00:27:48.560 --> 00:27:51.710
I admit I'm impressed
you made it this far.

357
00:27:51.710 --> 00:27:53.530
But this is the end for you, boy.

358
00:27:53.530 --> 00:27:56.400
And this land. Everything!

359
00:27:56.400 --> 00:27:58.660
I can easily create another Raigo!

360
00:28:02.990 --> 00:28:06.790
It's the duty of every
citizen here on the Island.

361
00:28:06.920 --> 00:28:08.330
I'm so very sorry!

362
00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:16.770
Will the sky islands
really be destroyed?

363
00:28:23.150 --> 00:28:26.360
So you prefer to fall, do you?

364
00:28:33.440 --> 00:28:34.230
Luffy, no!

365
00:28:36.190 --> 00:28:38.070
Nami. Get out of the way, hurry!

366
00:28:43.710 --> 00:28:44.880
What's this?

367
00:28:45.250 --> 00:28:48.080
You should never mess
with me, earlobes!

368
00:28:48.080 --> 00:28:52.540
Now, Gum-Gum... Rocket!

369
00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:57.920
Gum-Gum...

370
00:28:58.760 --> 00:29:01.680
Are you going to try
that same old trick again?

371
00:29:01.800 --> 00:29:04.010
I'll keep trying till the bell rings!

372
00:29:04.980 --> 00:29:06.690
This time I'll skewer you, fool!

373
00:29:06.690 --> 00:29:10.560
...Golden Rifle!

374
00:29:13.730 --> 00:29:14.480
Too fast!

375
00:29:33.120 --> 00:29:37.130
When you finally return, what will
you think when you see we're gone?

376
00:29:41.300 --> 00:29:42.610
Hold on a little longer!

377
00:29:42.610 --> 00:29:44.740
I'll let you know
that we're still here!

378
00:29:54.980 --> 00:29:56.230
Noland!

379
00:29:56.230 --> 00:29:58.860
Light the Fire of Shandora!

380
00:30:00.440 --> 00:30:05.270
The war in the sky began 400 years ago.

381
00:30:05.270 --> 00:30:08.980
I didn't think I'd
live to see this moment.

382
00:30:11.570 --> 00:30:14.870
Yes. The Holy Land...

383
00:30:19.410 --> 00:30:21.580
...will sing once more.

384
00:30:25.260 --> 00:30:27.930
Someday, it will.

385
00:30:40.190 --> 00:30:46.770
Six years ago, on the island of Jaya in
the Grand Line, I saw the City of Gold!

386
00:30:50.370 --> 00:30:53.540
The City of Gold does exist!

387
00:31:00.910 --> 00:31:07.130
Not one person in history has ever disproven,
heh, the existence of sky island.

388
00:31:08.730 --> 00:31:11.570
I'm a romantic! Just like you!

389
00:31:11.570 --> 00:31:15.160
Let it ring!

390
00:31:16.870 --> 00:31:18.200
Hey, Pops!

391
00:31:18.200 --> 00:31:19.700
Can you hear it?

392
00:31:20.650 --> 00:31:22.740
The City of Gold is here!

393
00:31:27.150 --> 00:31:30.100
For 400 years,

394
00:31:30.100 --> 00:31:31.760
the City of Gold...

395
00:31:32.260 --> 00:31:36.300
...has been in the sky!

396
00:31:44.360 --> 00:31:49.880
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

397
00:31:50.100 --> 00:31:55.300
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

398
00:31:55.300 --> 00:31:58.100
You are so much like the moon

399
00:31:58.100 --> 00:32:02.750
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

400
00:32:06.200 --> 00:32:15.150
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

401
00:32:15.210 --> 00:32:20.380
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

402
00:32:20.380 --> 00:32:28.690
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

403
00:32:29.330 --> 00:32:35.580
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

404
00:32:35.580 --> 00:32:41.200
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

405
00:32:42.440 --> 00:32:46.970
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

406
00:32:46.970 --> 00:32:53.360
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
